\section{Reflective Report}


\subsubsection{Compassion}
Compassion was clearly visible during our visit through the behavior of the temple volunteers. Despite the heavy festive crowd, they treated every visitor with patience and kindness. For example, even when people repeatedly asked for directions or assistance, the volunteers calmly guided them without showing frustration. This made us realize that compassion is not just about helping others, but doing so with genuine care and understanding.

\subsubsection{Responsibility}
Responsibility was demonstrated both by our team and the temple management. Each of us fulfilled our assigned roles sincerely, ensuring that the visit was smooth and well-coordinated. For instance, while interacting with the priest, we ensured discipline and did not interrupt or create disturbance. Similarly, the temple staff efficiently managed large crowds, showing how responsibility plays a key role in maintaining order and harmony.

\subsubsection{Cooperation}
Cooperation played a crucial role in the success of our visit. Due to the festive rush, there were delays and crowd-related challenges. However, as a team, we supported each other and adjusted accordingly. For example, while waiting for the interaction with the priest, we stayed together, coordinated our roles, and ensured that no confusion occurred. This highlighted the importance of teamwork in overcoming practical challenges.

\subsubsection{Patience}
Patience was an important value we experienced during the visit. Since it was a festive day, we had to wait longer than expected to interact with the priest. Instead of becoming restless, we remained calm and used the time to observe the surroundings and understand the temple environment. This situation taught us that patience helps in handling unexpected delays effectively without disrupting the overall experience.

\subsubsection{Respect}
Respect was maintained throughout the visit, both by our team and the temple staff. We ensured that we followed temple norms, maintained silence where required, and behaved appropriately in a spiritual setting. For example, during the interaction, we listened attentively to the priest without interrupting, showing respect for his time and knowledge. This helped us understand that respect is essential in building meaningful interactions and maintaining harmony in any environment.

